      "content": "# Task\nThe Python script `buggy.py` (your current directory) fails when run with **Qiskit 2.5.0**.\nIt comes from a user question titled: \"How to convert QuantumCircuit to OpenQasm 2.0 in qiskit 1.0+\"\n\nObserved error when running it on Qiskit 2.5.0:\n```\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"C:\\personal_webpage\\my-portfolio\\APR_code_gen\\Part2_Create_test\\reconstructed_cases\\apr_p30\\runs\\sonnet5.5p30\\tasks\\issue_036\\workspace\\buggy.py\", line 6, in <module>\r\n    qasm_str = c.qasm()\r\n               ^^^^^^\r\nAttributeError: 'QuantumCircuit' object has no attribute 'qasm'\r\n\n```\n\nRepair `buggy.py` **in place** so that it runs successfully on Qiskit 2.5.0\nand still does what the original author intended (same circuit / computation).\n\n## Rules\n- Run the script with `$PY buggy.py` (Qiskit 2.5.0 is installed only in that interpreter).\n  Do not pip install, downgrade or upgrade packages. There is no internet access from the shell.\n- Fix the root cause. Do NOT hide the error with try/except, do NOT delete the failing logic,\n  and do NOT replace the program with something unrelated.\n- Keep the change minimal. Plots may be produced, but the script must not block or need a display.\n\n## Workflow\n1. Read `buggy.py` and reproduce the error with `$PY buggy.py`.\n2. Work out why it fails on Qiskit 2.5.0.\n3. Edit `buggy.py` (e.g. with `cat <<'EOF' > buggy.py` or `sed -i`).\n4. Re-run `$PY buggy.py` until it exits with status 0.\n5. When done, submit by running exactly `echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT` as a separate command.\n   You cannot continue after submitting.\n\nEach command runs in a fresh subshell; `cd` and environment changes do not persist.\n\n\n## Original user question (solution sections removed)\nTitle: How to convert QuantumCircuit to OpenQasm 2.0 in qiskit 1.0+\n\nI need to convert a QuantumCircuit to a string of the equivalent OpenQasm 2.0 circuit in qiskit. \n It seems like the method .qasm() disappeared from the QuantumCircuit class in qiskit 1.0\nAnd I wasn't able to find an alternative. \n I need the qiskit 1.0 version of this: \n c = qiskit.QuantumCircuit(1)\nc.h(0)\n\nc.qasm()\n\n```\nc  = qiskit.QuantumCircuit(1)\nc.h(0)\n\nc.qasm()\n```\n\nOnly inspect and edit this task workspace and installed dependency APIs. Reference fixes, evaluation tests, other cases and previous repairs are unavailable inputs."
